<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sunni Baru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1492">1492</a>–<a href="/years/1493">1493</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Sonni Baru, Abu Bakr Dao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Baru was the last ruler of the Sunni dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-ali">Sunni Ali</a> in 1492. He reportedly refused to profess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> publicly, which alienated the Muslim scholars and merchants of the towns, and in April 1493 he was defeated near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao">Gao</a> by his father's general Muhammad Ture, who seized the throne as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askia-muhammad">Askia Muhammad</a> and founded the Askia dynasty.</p></div>
